description:
Accept stored original VLA joint steps, or track model-supplied TCP targets with internal measured-state feedback and IK. TCP targets use continuous gripper_opening (0 closed, 1 open). Supplying targets declines the proposal. Return status, actual native steps, residual errors, current RGB and measured TCP state. Inspect interrupted results before choosing another action; an interrupted VLA proposal cannot be reused. Pose arrival does not verify grasp. Keep reason/assessment concise. Only when observe reports review_due, act.review records legacy checkpoint analysis; it does not determine the native score.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__robot__act(args: {
  assessment: { current_subgoal: string; };
  // Shared native-step budget for TCP tracking, default 80. Omit for original VLA acceptance.
  max_native_steps?: number;
  // Copy the current short VLA proposal_id, e.g. p1; omit when supplying targets.
  proposal_id?: string;
  reason: string;
  // Legacy harness checkpoint record, only when observe reports review_due. These fields are not native scoring conditions. Without proposal_id/steps/targets, records the due checkpoint without motion.
  review?: { demo_comparison: string; ending_check: string; next_plan: string; observed_state: string; why_not_done: string; };
  // Consecutive prefix length; VLA allows 5..50, default 5.
  steps?: number;
  // Model-chosen dual-arm TCP waypoints; no proposal_id or reject flag. Harness tracks each to 3mm/3deg before advancing. A waypoint may consume multiple native steps; model-side interpolation is unnecessary.
  targets?: Array<{ left: {
  // Continuous normalized opening: 0 fully closed, 1 fully open.
  gripper_opening: number;
  // Degrees about environment +X, relative to the downward reference.
  pitch_deg: number;
  // Absolute gripping-face-centre TCP XYZ in environment-origin metres.
  position: Array<number>;
  // Degrees about environment +Y, applied after pitch.
  roll_deg: number;
  // Degrees about environment +Z, applied after roll.
  yaw_deg: number;
}; right: {
  // Continuous normalized opening: 0 fully closed, 1 fully open.
  gripper_opening: number;
  // Degrees about environment +X, relative to the downward reference.
  pitch_deg: number;
  // Absolute gripping-face-centre TCP XYZ in environment-origin metres.
  position: Array<number>;
  // Degrees about environment +Y, applied after pitch.
  roll_deg: number;
  // Degrees about environment +Z, applied after roll.
  yaw_deg: number;
}; }>;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```
